Deterministic seed fragment for the MODEL HUB installed-models list.

Unblocks the desktop Model Hub automation (model-hub-det.json):
  * installed-models-section            (ModelHub.svelte, always present)
  * installed-models-total              (rendered only when >= 1 model)
  * installed-models-list               (rendered only when >= 1 model)
  * installed-model-row-{name}          (one per .gguf/.bin file, nth 0 = Phi)
  * installed-model-size-{name}         (formatted file size)
  * installed-model-inuse-{name}        (only when a backend/STT references the file)
  * installed-model-delete-{name}       (delete button; disabled when in_use)
  * installed-model-delete-dialog       (opens on click of an ENABLED delete button)
  * installed-model-delete-dialog-confirm / -cancel

This is NOT a database seed. Installed models are files on disk, not rows.
The builder must COPY the two files under files/models/ into the seeded home:

    <SEED_HOME>/.apollia/models/Phi-3-mini-Q4.gguf
    <SEED_HOME>/.apollia/models/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-MXFP4_MOE.gguf

(Create <SEED_HOME>/.apollia/models/ first, then copy. No system.db write is
performed by this fragment.)

--- What the scanner requires (traced) -------------------------------------

Source: crates/apollia-desktop/src/commands/model_hub.rs, fn
collect_installed_models (list_installed_models command).

The scanner reads models_dir() = <HOME>/.apollia/models/ with std::fs::read_dir
and, per entry:
  1. keeps it only if path.is_file();
  2. classifies by extension ONLY: "gguf" -> Llm, "bin" -> Stt, else skipped;
  3. reads size via entry.metadata().len();
  4. takes the basename as the display name;
  5. sorts the list by name ascending (bytewise): out.sort_by(a.name.cmp(b.name)).

Requirement = STAT ONLY (name + extension + size). The scanner NEVER opens the
file and NEVER parses the GGUF magic/header. It does NOT detect sharded models
(*-00001-of-0000N.gguf), projectors (mmproj*), or sidecar/manifest files. A
model appears as an installed row from a single correctly-named *.gguf file.

Therefore a tiny placeholder is enough. As a low-cost hedge (in case any other
code path ever opens these files), each placeholder still begins with a valid
empty GGUF v3 header: magic "GGUF" | version u32=3 | tensor_count u64=0 |
metadata_kv_count u64=0, zero-padded to a small size. This parses as a valid
(empty) GGUF but is never loaded by the Model Hub view.

--- File layout ------------------------------------------------------------

  Phi-3-mini-Q4.gguf              4096 bytes  (nth 0, NOT in use, deletable)
  Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-MXFP4_MOE.gguf  8192 bytes  (nth 1, in use, delete disabled)

Ordering matters. Rows sort by name ascending. "Phi" (ASCII 'P' 0x50) sorts
before "Qwen" (ASCII 'Q' 0x51), so Phi is nth 0. model-hub-det.json clicks
installed-model-delete- at nth 0 and expects the delete dialog to open; the
delete button is disabled when in_use, so the nth-0 row MUST be the NOT-in-use
model. The automation cancels the dialog (boundary only), so no file is ever
removed and the seed stays idempotent across re-runs.

--- In-use badge (cross-agent coordination) --------------------------------

installed-model-inuse-{name} renders only when an LLM backend or the STT config
in <SEED_HOME>/.apollia/system.db references the SAME basename (conservative
basename match, model_hub.rs used_by / collect_in_use_refs). system.db is owned
by the llm-backends seed agent; this fragment only places the files.

For the Qwen row to show "in use", the llm-backends seed must register a backend
whose model (or config_json.model_path basename) equals exactly:

    Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-MXFP4_MOE.gguf

If that backend is absent, the inuse waitFor simply fails (model-hub-det.json
runs with stopOnError:false) and both rows become deletable; the delete-dialog
boundary step still passes because the nth-0 (Phi) button stays enabled.
